  "raw": {
    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4582?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Athletic Training)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Athletic Training) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor (Athletic Training) Lafayette, LA | req4582 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/7/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Assistant Professor (Athletic Training) Department : 2340|Kinesiology Responsibilities : POSITION: Assistant Professor in Athletic Training\n(MSAT), School of Kinesiology, University of Louisiana at Lafayette, nine-month\ntenure track appointment. This position will report to the Director of the School of Kinesiology. RESPONSIBILITIES: A tenure track faculty member is expected to Excel in\nteaching, develop a strong research agenda, engage in service, and be an active\nteam member to advance the School of Kinesiology in alignment with our vision\nand mission. Work with colleagues to\ncontinually assess and improve the CAATE accredited program. Teaching focus\nwill center on MSAT program needs with the possibility of undergraduate\nkinesiology courses housed in the Pre-Athletic Training concentration. Assist with student advising in the Pre-Athletic Training concentration. ADMINISTRATIVE UNIT: UL Lafayette (R1) is the largest of nine publicly\nsupported universities in the University of Louisiana system with an enrollment\nof approximately 19,000 students (as of fall 2025). The School of Kinesiology\nhouses both graduate (M.S. in Athletic Training and Kinesiology) and\nundergraduate programs (B.S. Health and Physical Education, Exercise Science,\nSport Management, Health Promotion and Wellness) with over a total of 1000 enrolled\nstudents. The facilities include a 1500+ sq. ft. human performance laboratory\nand athletic training laboratory. For further details on laboratory equipment\nplease contact the search committee chair. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: -Earned doctorate in Athletic Training, Kinesiology, or a related discipline. ABD eligible to apply. -An understanding of CAATE standards and integration of standards into teaching as well as assessment activities -Teaching experience (didactic or clinical education experiences) -Previous or current experience with clinical practice as a certified athletic trainer -Evidence of\n     a successful applied research and scholarship agenda -Certification\n     and good standing with the Board of Certification for the Athletic Trainer\n     (BOC) -Eligible for\n     obtaining licensure or currently licensed in the state of Louisiana as an\n     athletic trainer (LSBME) -If selected candidate is ABD, they will be hired at the\nrank of Instructor, with the requirement that the candidate finish the doctoral\ndegree within the first year of employment . Preferred Qualifications: -BOC certification for five years or longer -Clinical practice as an athletic trainer for five years or longer -Greater than three years of college-level teaching -Experience with distance learning instruction -Prior experience with CAATE accreditation process -Record of inter-professional collaboration in curriculum development and/or research -History of extramural funding or potential for funding -Demonstrated professional service at state, regional, national, and/or international levels. -Contemporary expertise in Domain 4 (therapeutic intervention) content established by BOC. -Availability for summer teaching (online or in person). SALARY: Negotiable commensurate with qualifications, rank, and\nexperience. STARTING DATE: January 4, 2027 APPLICATION MATERIALS: Applications should be submitted electronically and will\ninclude: Cover letter describing your qualifications for the position Complete, well-organized curriculum vitae Statement of past, present, and future research focus Teaching philosophy Three professional references: please include name, title, institution \nof employment, email and phone contact information for each    \n reference Copies of unofficial transcripts from all degree granting institutions, official transcripts will be needed upon hire. Job Ad# (req4582) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
    },
    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4595?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Class Analyst",
      "description": "Class Analyst | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Class Analyst Lafayette, LA, United States | req4595 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/6/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Class Analyst Department : 9020|Picard Center for Child Dev Responsibilities : POSITION: CLASS Analyst START DATE: TBD RESPONSIBILITIES: The CLASS Analyst will work under the direction of the CLASS Project Director. This individual should demonstrate strong communication skills, work efficiently with attention to detail while meeting deadlines under pressure. This individual should be a self-starter, a problem-solver, adaptable, and work collaboratively with CLASS grant team. Most importantly, this individual should be out-going and share joy in speaking or interacting with people through-out their workday. •In collaboration with the CLASS Project Coordinator, who completes the observation scheduling, the individual will lead communication between the observation sites and management. •Provide expert guidance to observers visiting schools, Head Start centers, or child care centers and confer with administration should problems arise. •Provide accurate and ongoing support to CLASS observers for planning and executing CLASS observations. •Review the quality and accuracy of observational data entered into the LDOE’s Early Childhood Observation System (ECOS) and cross-check with observation booklets, as needed. •Attend LDOE/Picard Center staff meetings with support documentation. •Plan and present at the annual orientation. •Participate in one CLASS observation training (infant-toddler or PreK-3rd) and pass the reliability test. •Recruit observers for observations by reviewing qualifications, interviewing, and onboarding. •Provide support to the Project Director and Early Childhood team by participating in cross-training. •Assist with boxing and storing completed observation booklets (must be able to lift up to 25 lbs.). SALARY: $40,000-$45,000 Qualifications: Required Qualifications: •Education: Bachelor’s Degree Skills, Abilities, Etc: •Exceptional professional communication and organizational skills •Experience working in a busy, fast-paced environment •Coordinating and executing the daily activities of a large-scale project •Skilled proofreader •Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, and Power Point •CLASS certification preferred Job Ad# (req4595) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
