    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4586?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Enrollment Specialist",
      "description": "Enrollment Specialist | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Enrollment Specialist Lafayette, LA | req4586 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/5/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Enrollment Specialist Department : 2032|Distance Learning Responsibilities : In the Office of Distance Learning at the University of Louisiana at Lafayette, the Enrollment Specialist will create and build relationships with prospective students to assist them in incorporating online learning into their busy lives. The ideal candidate will maintain frequent communication with prospective and current online students, as well as those who have stopped-out in order to influence enrollment and retention in online programs. This position reports to an Assistant Program Manager. Duties and Responsibilities: * Work to build relationships with each prospective and current student and learn their career aspirations so as to advise them on the best online degree for their goals and how to incorporate online learning into their life. * Produce timely and effective responses to student inquiries leading to increased applicants for all hybrid and online programs. * Maintain consistent phone, text, and/or email communication with prospective and current students to assist students from the inquiry phase through graduation. * Collaborate with appropriate departments, such as Undergraduate Admissions, Graduate School, Financial Aid, Registrar, Bursar and other support services to resolve individual student issues and ensure positive student experiences. * Ensure admitted online students have taken the necessary steps to start their program (ie., students have completed online orientation, advising, registration, financial aid processing). Advise the student in overcoming barriers to registering. * Deliver strategic, individualized retention strategies to ensure student persistence and student academic success targets are met. * Coach students as needed throughout their degree program. * Track student enrollment, persistence, success, and completion. Produce reports as needed. * Develop tools and strategies to remove common challenges online students encounter. * Develop tools and strategies to make the inquiry to graduation process smoother for our online students as well as the Distance Learning Office and staff. * Adapt work schedule as needed to support our working adult population * Perform related duties as necessary to support the UL Lafayette Office of Distance Learning mission, goals, and objectives. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: -Bachelor’s degree -2 years experience in student advising, enrollment management, customer service, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications: -Industry Based Certification in Professional Coaching, Communication, Leadership, Mentoring, and/or Problem Solving -Familiarity with academic affairs policies and issues -Experience working on student support initiatives -Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills -Effective listening, assessment, and problem-solving skills -Strong time management and organizational skills -Ability to thrive in a rapidly changing, dynamic, and deadline-driven environment -Ability to serve a diversity of backgrounds, cultures, talents, and experiences -Ability to work independently and present creative ideas within an interdependent team -Ability to operate within customer relationship management systems and complex computer databases -High attention to detail with the ability to manage multiple ongoing activities. Application Requirements:  cover letter, resume, and (3) professional references including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address Job Ad# (req4586) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
