    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4483?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Communications Specialist - Social Media",
      "description": "Communications Specialist - Social Media | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Communications Specialist - Social Media Lafayette, LA | req4483 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/5/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Communications Specialist - Social Media Department : 2032|Distance Learning Responsibilities : Reporting to the Assistant Director of Marketing and Communications Manager in the Office of Distance Learning, the Communications Specialist – Social Media will plan, develop, and schedule social media content across UL Lafayette Online’s channels and provide strategic support to departmental stakeholders. This position will also support operational goals in developing, writing, and editing accurate, accessible, and customer focused messages for all Office of Distance Learning units while coordinating with appropriate staff in UL Lafayette’s Office of Communications and Marketing. Duties and Responsibilities: The Communication Specialist – Social Media will: Build and execute social media strategy for UL Lafayette Online through competitive and audience research. Monitor social media trends and find unique ways to integrate them into the brand. Consistently generate, edit, and publish content (original text, images, graphics, and short-form video) that facilitates engagement and encourages conversion. Collaborate with stakeholders to ensure content is relevant and consistent with brand standards. Maintain current knowledge of social media updates and best practices. Optimize UL Lafayette Online channels to increase visibility, using data insights and best practices. Manage user-generated content in accordance with University and departmental policies. Develop social media calendars internally and for stakeholder departments. Ensure content meets current accessibility guidelines and is aligned with marketing goals. Proactively monitor and respond to audience engagement across social media platforms, including comments and messages, while maintaining brand voice and fostering positive relationships with audiences. Report monthly on relevant performance metrics. Develop news and blog content for UL Lafayette Online’s website, as needed. Perform related duties as necessary to support the UL Lafayette Office of Distance Learning mission, goals, and objectives. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Education: A bachelor’s degree in communications, journalism, English, marketing, technical writing, or a bachelor’s degree in a non-related field accompanied by a portfolio of work demonstrating significant experience and preferred skills. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Must be an exceptional writer with: Experience as a social media specialist or similar position Excellent critical thinking, interpersonal communication, time-management and problem-solving skills. A storytelling-first creative mindset. Ability to use social media for engagement and brand awareness. Excellent knowledge of social media platforms including Facebook, Instagram, and TikTok. Understanding of social media KPIs, web traffic metrics and SEO. Experience conducting audience research and developing personas. Demonstrated knowledge of online content strategy, accessibility standards and principles, and SEO approaches. Demonstrable skills in persuasive communication with the ability to incorporate a diversity of backgrounds, cultures, talents, and experiences when developing content for different audiences. Ability to work independently and within a team. Ability to meet strict deadlines. Application Requirements: cover letter, resume, the names and contact information of three references, and a digital work portfolio*. *Practicum may be requested in lieu of portfolio. Job Ad# (req4483) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
    },
    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4532?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Academic Advisor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Academic Advisor Lafayette, LA | req4532 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/21/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Academic Advisor Department : 2010|Academic Success Center Responsibilities : The University of Louisiana at Lafayette is seeking a dynamic professional to serve as an Academic Advisor within the Academic Success Center to facilitate professional academic advising services to first year students . The Academic Success Center is part of the division of Student Success. The Academic Success Center's Academic Advisors take a holistic approach in the responsibilities of: providing academic and career planning to first year students, coaching students on high impact academic success practices, informing students of degree requirements and supporting their transition into college.   The advisor will support the ASC’s and University’s efforts to increase the persistence and graduation rates of the undergraduate student by fostering retention of students through mentoring, advising, and other support programs. DUTIES: -Advise assigned students on progression requirements and selection of courses. Review and interpret placement and other standardized test scores, transcripts, courses enrollment and other transfer work. -Maintain systematic and frequent contact with advisees. -Monitor, identify, and support students with academic difficulties. -Refer students to appropriate support services such as counseling, financial aid, etc. and encourage student participation in beyond the classroom activities. -Collaborate with academic college and departmental representatives to ensure understanding of all degree programs responsible for advising. -Provide an open and welcoming atmosphere that respects the unique and diverse background of each student. -Support students through the development of career goals. -Maintain thorough knowledge of major-specific curriculum and co-curricular activities. -Serve on appropriate department, college and/or campus advisory committees. -Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: -Master’s Degree from a regionally accredited institution of higher learning. -Minimum of two years of work experience in higher education, preferably in academic advising, or counseling. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: -Ability to work as part of a mutually dependent and supportive team. -Demonstrated commitment to diversity and to supporting the academic success of all students. -Excellent communication skills, strong interpersonal skills, ability to remain calm under pressure and to adapt quickly to change. -Working knowledge of ERP system (i.e. Banner) or demonstrated ability to learn and utilize student data management system. A cover letter stating why you are interested in this specific position and your qualifications, in addition to a CV or resume, are required in order to be considered for the position.    Please submit your cover letter and resume as one PDF document. Job Ad# (req4532) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
    },
