    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4578?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Director of Institutional Research",
      "description": "Director of Institutional Research | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Director of Institutional Research Lafayette, LA | req4578 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/19/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Director of Institutional Research Department : 2030|Institutional Research Responsibilities : The Director of Institutional Research serves as a visionary, service-minded intelligence leader and trusted advisor to campus executives. The Director leads the transformation of institutional data into actionable, forward-looking insights that drive strategic growth, institutional effectiveness, as program, faculty, and student success. Grounded in a culture of collaborative service and relationship-building, this role bridges business intelligence with institutional strategy, fostering strong cross-functional partnerships, championing proactive decision-making, and navigating the evolving higher education landscape. DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Visionary Leadership & Relationship Building Strategic Partnership: Build trust-based, collaborative relationships across academic and administrative units, deans, and campus leaders to proactively identify data needs and deliver consultative insights. Cross-Institutional Alignment: Partner actively with IR offices across the UL System and external networks to benchmark innovative practices, harmonize data definitions, and champion collaborative higher education research. Strategic Data Translation & Storytelling: Guide the synthesis, analysis, and compelling presentation of complex data into clear, actionable resources, reports, and high-impact special projects for executive leadership and campus stakeholders—translating raw metrics into meaningful strategic narratives. Service-Minded Culture: Cultivate a customer-centric, accessible, and supportive environment within the Office of IR, positioning the team as a go-to partner for strategic problem-solving. Coalition & Governance Leadership: Chair and guide key governance groups, including the Data Governance Committee, Data Standards Committee, and work with data visualization experts to inspire shared data stewardship and collaborative decision-making. Serve as a member of the Data Governance Committee, as well as represent the Office of IR in meetings or committees for institutional reporting and data needs. Strategic Intelligence & Forward-Thinking Analytics Predictive & Proactive Insights: Shift institutional research from historical reporting to forward-thinking predictive modeling, trend forecasting, and scenario planning to anticipate institutional opportunities and risks. Modern Business Intelligence: Drive the expansion of modern data visualization tools (e.g., Tableau) and interactive dashboards to empower campus stakeholders with self-service analytics and KPI tracking. Digital Presence & Data Transparency: Oversee the IR website to ensure it serves as a dynamic, user-friendly hub for institutional intelligence; curate public-facing dashboards, fact books, accountability metrics, and strategic plan tracking; and maintain accessible resources that promote campus-wide data literacy. Environmental Scanning: Synthesize higher education trends, demographic shifts, and regional benchmarks to inform long-range strategic planning and enrollment strategies. Data Enablement & Campus Literacy: Design and lead campus-wide training programs, workshops, and user-friendly resources that empower faculty, staff, and leadership to effectively navigate analytics platforms (e.g., Tableau, Qualtrics, Ellucian Insight), interpret data accurately, and build confidence in data-informed decision-making. Data Strategy, Governance & Ecosystem Modernization Ethical Data Stewardship & Integrity: Collaborate with the Enterprise Data Governance Planning Committee to establish modern data standards, ethical AI/data usage policies, and robust security controls. Ensure appropriate, ethical, and compliant use of data on behalf of the university. Embed the standard of ethical practice as defined by AIR. ( https://www.airweb.org/resources/publications/statement-of-ethical-principles/principles ) Data Infrastructure Elevation: Guide the continuous optimization of data pipelines, operational data storage systems, and analytics platforms to ensure seamless data delivery, both internally and with system partners. Strategic Survey Administration & Governance: Oversee the campus-wide scheduling, design, and administration of institutional surveys using enterprise tools (Qualtrics); enforce policy compliance, survey fatigue mitigation, and best practices; and govern the appropriate use of institutional distribution lists to safeguard data integrity and student/employee privacy. Mandatory & Regulatory Excellence: Direct accurate and timely compliance reporting (Board of Regents, NCES/IPEDS, U.S. News, external rankings) and serve as the primary liaison for System-level shared resources. Coordinate campus data validation, subject-matter expertise, approvals and institutional context to ensure accurate and timely submissions. Team Development & Operational Stewardship Professional Thought Leadership & Horizon Scanning: Actively engage with regional and national professional associations (e.g., AIR, SAIR, LAIR) through conference attendance, network participation, and scholarly research to track emerging higher education trends, modern analytics methodologies, and advanced IR technologies—ensuring the university remains at the forefront of data-informed leadership. Project Management & Tracking: Prioritize and manage data requests through clear intake criteria; track and communicate project milestones transparently to stakeholders; and foster a culture of continuous operational improvement. Talent Empowerment: Mentor and develop a modern, growth-oriented IR team, fostering a supportive, innovative, and continuous-learning workplace culture. Resource Management: Strategically deploy financial and technological resources to maximize the impact of the IR office on campus priorities. Qualifications: Required Qualifications Master’s degree in a relevant field, such as informatics, statistical analysis, research methodology, social sciences, or a related field. Three to five years of experience working in a university setting and using institutional data to support program improvement, faculty effectiveness, and student success. Experience leading teams, managing budgets, coordinating multiple projects and reporting requirements, and effectively managing competing priorities and deadlines across university units. Experience collecting, managing, analyzing, and reporting institutional data. Ability to translate complex data into clear, understandable information and provide actionable analysis to university stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in a relevant field, such as informatics, statistical analysis, research methodology, social sciences, or a related field. Experience with data analysis and reporting tools within higher education. Job Ad# (req4578) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
    },
    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4525?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Software Quality Assurance Analyst",
      "description": "Software Quality Assurance Analyst | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Software Quality Assurance Analyst Lafayette, LA | req4525 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/4/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Software Quality Assurance Analyst Department : 9030|IRI-Tech Transfer Responsibilities : The Software Quality Assurance Analyst plays an important role in ensuring the\nquality and reliability of IRI software products. They are responsible for\ndesigning and executing test plans, identifying and reporting bugs, and\ncollaborating with developers to resolve issues. The Software Quality Assurance Analyst reports to the Chief Technology Officer of the Informatics Research Institute\n(IRI). This is an on-site position in Lafayette, Louisiana. Duties and Responsibilities: -Define test objectives and scope;\n     develop test plans and test cases; identify and prioritize test scenarios. -Execute test cases manually or\n     using automated testing tools; reproduce and document bugs and defects; track\n     and report test progress. -Log and categorize bugs using\n     defect tracking systems; communicate bugs to developers and track their\n     resolution; verify bug fixes and ensure they do not introduce new issues. -Collaborate with developers to\n     understand software requirements and design; communicate test results and\n     findings to stakeholders; participate in development meetings and provide\n     feedback. -Conduct usability testing; evaluate\n     software usability and user experience; identify and report usability\n     issues and suggest improvements; ensure software is user-friendly and accessible. -Ensure product design\n     consistency; verifies that UI/UX adheres to IRI guidelines and design principles to ensure consistent customer\n     experience. -Conduct performance testing; assess\n     software performance under load; identify and report performance\n     bottlenecks; optimize software performance for scalability and\n     responsiveness. -Conduct security testing; identify\n     and assess security vulnerabilities; conduct penetration testing to\n     identify potential exploits; recommend security measures and best\n     practices. -Develop documentation; maintain\n     and update test plans, test cases, and test results; document defect\n     reports and resolution procedures; create and maintain user guides and\n     training materials. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: -Bachelor’s degree in computer science or related field. -Or 5 years of work experience in software development in real\n     world settings may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree. Preferred Qualifications: -Proficiency in\n     at least one of the following programming languages: Java, C#, Python, or\n     C++. -Understanding of various testing methodologies,\n     including black-box testing, white-box testing, exploratory testing, and\n     automated testing. -Analytical and conceptual thinking skills; ability to\n     meticulously examine software products and identify potential defects;\n     ability to analyze problems, identify root causes, and develop effective\n     solutions; ability to apply logical thinking to understand software\n     behavior and identify inconsistencies. -Ability to clearly articulate test findings, defects,\n     and suggestions to developers and stakeholders. -Ability to work effectively with developers, project\n     managers, and other stakeholders to resolve issues and ensure quality\n     software delivery. -Proficiency in using various testing tools and frameworks, such as Selenium, JUnit, and TestNG. -Knowledge of Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) phases and the role of QA testing within the SDLC. -Excellent verbal and\n     written communication skills; ability\n     to write clear, concise, and informative documentation, such as test\n     plans, defect reports, and user guides. -Excellent planning, documentation,\n     and organizational skills. -Competency in Microsoft\n     applications including Word, Excel, and Outlook. Job Ad# (req4525) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
