    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4507?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Vice President for Advancement and Strategy",
      "description": "Vice President for Advancement and Strategy | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Vice President for Advancement and Strategy Lafayette, LA | req4507 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/4/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Vice President for Advancement and Strategy Department : 7000|VP University Advancement Responsibilities : Position Summary The University of Louisiana at Lafayette, an R1\nnational research university, seeks an experienced, collaborative, and mission-aligned Vice President for Advancement & Strategy\n(VPAS) to lead the University’s external partnerships, institutional brand, and\nrevenue-generating initiatives. Reporting directly to the President and serving\non the President’s Cabinet, the VPAS is responsible for converting the\nUniversity’s academic, research, innovation, and brand strengths into\nmeasurable economic impact, private investment, philanthropic support, and\nsustained revenue growth. This role integrates advancement, economic\ndevelopment, industry partnerships, communications and marketing, and alumni\naffairs under a single strategic leader. The VPAS serves as the University’s\nchief convener with industry, investors, alumni, and community leaders,\nensuring alignment between strategy, execution, and outcomes. Key Responsibilities -University and Advancement/Economic\nDevelopment Strategy -Serve as a senior adviser to the President on university strategy, advancement strategy, external positioning, partnership opportunities, and revenue-generating initiatives. -Lead university-wide strategic planning initiatives and facilitate cross-functional collaboration among academic, research, finance, advancement, communications, athletics, alumni, and external partners. -Lead an integrated advancement and strategy portfolio that supports the President’s priorities and University-wide goals. Advancement\n& Fundraising Coordination -Work in close coordination with the CEO of the University Foundation, development officers, and the advancement team to align priorities with University strategy. -Support the cultivation of corporate, foundation, and individual donors for major University priorities. -Connect economic development initiatives, industry partnerships, alumni engagement, and strategic priorities with major gifts, corporate giving, foundation support, and campaign objectives. Communications, Marketing and Brand Strategy -Provide executive oversight of the Office of Communications & Marketing through the Chief Communications Officer. -Ensure a cohesive institutional brand narrative aligned with the University’s mission, strategy, research strengths, student experience, alumni pride, and regional role. -Position the University as a leading institution in research, innovation, entrepreneurship, economic development, student success, and community partnership. -Ensure communications and marketing strategies support philanthropy, alumni pride, partnership development, enrollment strength, reputation, and presidential priorities. -Actively pursue revenue opportunities related to licensing, brand partnerships, and sponsorships. Alumni & Government Affairs -Provide executive oversight of Alumni Affairs through the Executive Director of Alumni Affairs. -Strengthen engagement by mobilizing alumni as donors, partners, investors, advocates, mentors, ambassadors, and supporters of university priorities. -Align alumni programming with advancement strategy, institutional priorities, economic development opportunities, and external partnerships. -Support engagement with federal, state, and local agencies in coordination with the President and designated government relations offices. -Advance select agency partnerships when directly tied to major initiatives or investments. Economic\nDevelopment -Align and articulate the University’s academic, research, innovation, and brand strengths into measurable economic impact, private investment, philanthropic support, and sustained revenue growth. -Advance innovation districts, research parks, incubators, accelerators, and place-based development initiatives. -Partner with regional and statewide economic development organizations to attract, retain, and grow high-value employers and strategic partners. Capital Formation & Revenue\nGeneration -Identify, develop, and execute revenue strategies including but not limited to: public-private partnerships, leases, service agreements, sponsorships, and licensing. -Provide strategic support to the Office of Finance and Administration’s revenue initiatives with Auxiliary and campus units, including property management, KRVS, Hilliard Museum, UL Press, etc. -Support capital projects that generate long-term institutional returns and advance University priorities. -Collaborate with Finance, Advancement, Research, Legal, and campus leadership to ensure disciplined execution, risk management, and financial stewardship. Leadership &\nCollaboration -Serve on the President’s Cabinet. -Collaborate closely with Academic Affairs, Research & Innovation, Finance, Student Success, Athletics, and Advancement. -Lead and develop high-performing teams across economic development, partnerships, communications, and alumni engagement. -Ensure clear coordination across units whose work affects philanthropy, reputation, revenue, partnerships, alumni relations, economic development, and presidential priorities. -Represent the University with professionalism, credibility, and strategic clarity among donors, alumni, industry leaders, public officials, community partners, and institutional stakeholders. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: -Master’s degree required; terminal degree preferred. -Senior leadership experience in higher education, economic development, innovation, industry, government, or a related field. -Demonstrated success in strategic planning, delivering measurable outcomes through partnerships, and external engagement. -Strong strategic planning, financial, negotiation, and strategic execution skills. Preferred Qualifications: -Experience with R1 research universities, economic development and innovation ecosystems. -Track record in public-private partnerships, capital projects, and revenue-generating initiatives. -Established relationships with industry, investors, philanthropic partners, and community leaders. Job Ad# (req4507) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
    },
    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4442?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Child Care Center Teacher",
      "description": "Child Care Center Teacher | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Child Care Center Teacher Lafayette, LA | req4442 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/4/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Child Care Center Teacher Department : 3000|VP Student Affairs Responsibilities : The Child Care Center Teacher is responsible\nfor developing and implementing a rich teaching and learning environment for\nchildren, maintaining an organized and safe environment, and implementing daily\nactivities that are developmentally appropriate. The Child Development Center\nDirector will oversee and lead the Child Care Center Teacher in the\nimplementation of the daily activities and ensure compliance with state\nlicensing regulations and guidelines. Key Responsibilities: -Planning and implementing daily program of\ndevelopmentally appropriate activities  based on Louisiana Department\nof Education Early Learning Guidelines. -Planning and gathering necessary tools\n(documentation, TS Gold, etc)  to assess the needs of the individual child\nfor curriculum planning -Maintaining program quality, adhering to all\nstate licensing agencies and required regulations -Possessing knowledge of Teaching Strategies GOLD,\nLouisiana Pathways, CLASS assessment system, research-based best practices,\ndevelopmentally appropriate practices -Reviewing each child’s progress and develop plan\nto promote each child’s growth and development -Maintaining positive relationships with children\nand families with open communication concerning all aspects of the child’s\ndevelopment and by responding appropriately to their interests, requests, and\nneeds -Mentoring student interns -Attending/completing required trainings mandated\nby state licensing and the university -Maintaining records of children’s progress -Maintaining confidentiality of information -Preparing for special events; including, but not\nlimited to, holidays, dress-up days, deadline dates, parent-teacher\nconferences, scholastic book fair week, picture days, staff work/planning days,\nHomecoming parade, Mardi Gras parade, Winter Wonderland, Spring Fling, Pre-K\ncelebration, special guests, awareness activities, etc Qualifications: Required Qualifications: -At least 5 months of experience in an early\nlearning center or working directly with young children Preferred\nQualifications: -Technical Degree/Associate’s Degree/Bachelor’s\nDegree -Child Development Associate (CDA) certification -Must have, or be able to obtain, the Louisiana\nDepartment of Education Early Childhood Ancillary Certificate Job Ad# (req4442) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
