    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4494?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Server Administrator",
      "description": "Server Administrator | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Server Administrator Lafayette, LA | req4494 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/7/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Server Administrator Department : 9030|IRI-Tech Transfer Responsibilities : The Server\nAdministrator at the Informatics Research Institute at the University of\nLouisiana at Lafayette is responsible for the administration, support, and\ncontinuous improvement of enterprise applications and server environments. This\nposition provides technical leadership in application deployment, system\nintegration, security, disaster recovery planning, and performance management.\nThe role works closely with business and technical stakeholders to ensure\nreliable, secure, and efficient system operations while supporting upgrades,\nenhancements, troubleshooting, documentation, and user training activities. The Server\nAdministrator reports to the Chief Technology Officer of the Informatics\nResearch Institute. This is an on-site position in Baton Rouge, Louisiana. Duties and Responsibilities: Provide advanced expertise for the administration, configuration, and support of applications. Architect application deployment processes and strategies that align with State standards for application monitoring, lifecycle management, failover disaster recovery, and security. Provide expertise with integration with State Enterprise Architecture Services, specific APIs, identity management, document repositories, and related services. Design application-specific failover process and strategies to ensure services align with defined Service Level Agreements. Develop integration strategies and validation processes such that audit capabilities are incorporated and easily utilized. Coordinate enhancement, modifications or upgrades with users, developers, business analysts, infrastructure teams, governance groups, and change management teams with a goal of aligning testing processes. Produce documentation related to the provisioning, maintenance, and support of the system. Produce roll-back procedures and information related to validation and components. Provide training to new users and take the lead when troubleshooting system problems. Ensure process control activities are aligned with system performance. Perform additional duties as assigned. Qualifications: Required\nQualifications: Five (5) plus years advanced level experience in a Windows Server environment including performance tuning, database migrations, automation of complex application deployments or health checks using Python or advanced PowerShell. Expert-level knowledge of Windows Server OS and IIS; proficiency in PowerShell for service automation and log parsing. A Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Management Information Systems (MIS), or related. Preferred\nQualifications: A graduate degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Management Information Systems (MIS), or related. Relevant industry certifications such as ITIL Foundation, MS Windows Server Hybrid Administrator Associate, etc. Experience working on a development team. Experience with client engagements on design, delivery, deployment and on-going maintenance. Previous experience working in an Agile/Scrum environment. Experience managing Azure Cloud applications and services (IaaS and SaaS). Job Ad# (req4494) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
    },
    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4155?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Clinical Laboratory Scientist",
      "description": "Clinical Laboratory Scientist | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Clinical Laboratory Scientist New Iberia, LA, United States | req4155 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/22/2025 Back to Search Position Title : Clinical Laboratory Scientist Department : 9010|NIRC Administration Responsibilities : The New Iberia Research Center (NIRC), a premier $75 million biomedical research facility, supports groundbreaking research aimed at solving human health and societal challenges using non-human primates. As a resource for the global biomedical community, the NIRC provides the infrastructure and expertise required for innovative basic and applied research. The Clinical Laboratory Scientist plays a critical role in supporting these efforts by processing, analyzing, and reporting diagnostic samples to ensure research integrity and compliance with applicable regulations. Key Responsibilities: -Perform diagnostic testing in disciplines such as hematology, coagulation, chemistry, microbiology, flow cytometry, parasitology, and urinalysis. -Process, analyze, and report diagnostic samples in compliance with Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and applicable research regulations. -Conduct calibration, preventative maintenance, and quality control for laboratory equipment to ensure accurate and reliable results. -Manage and oversee the shipping of diagnostic samples, adhering to all regulatory and safety standards. -Maintain accurate records of laboratory analyses and quality control activities. -Perform analytical testing and processing in compliance with Standard Operating Procedures and applicable regulations -Collaborate with the Quality Assurance Auditor and other team members to uphold the highest standards of research integrity. -Participate in laboratory audits, inspections, and reviews as required. -Contribute to the development and implementation of new diagnostic methods and protocols. -Train and mentor laboratory staff and provide guidance on best practices. This position is integral to the mission of the NIRC, ensuring that its research activities are conducted with precision, quality, and adherence to the highest ethical standards. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: -A Bachelor of Science degree in Medical Technology or related field -Louisiana State licensure (or eligibility) as a Clinical Laboratory Scientist Preferred Qualifications: -A.S.C.P. certified or equivalent -Previous experience as a generalist in a biomedical research or clinical laboratory Skills, Knowledge, Abilities, Etc.: -Strong computer skills are a must, as are skills in managing, planning, and organizing multiple activities. -Basic knowledge and understanding of regulations governing operation of a research laboratory or hospital laboratory Job Ad# (req4155) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
