    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4572?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Career Coordinator",
      "description": "Career Coordinator | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Career Coordinator Lafayette, LA | req4572 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/10/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Career Coordinator Job Description Department : UL LIFE Responsibilities : Career Coordinator job duties and expectations are outlined below: Program & Policy Compliance Follow UL LIFE, University, and Think College policies and use resources accordingly Assist in accreditation efforts by developing or providing required documentation Follow Graduation Checklist with graduating cohort Respond to critical situations promptly and report all concerns, including personnel matters, to the Director Track and report PD (Professional Development) and supply spending Supervision & Recruitment Oversee assigned graduate assistant(s), including those supporting Employment Recruit and support peer mentors Curriculum, Courses & Advising Coordinate, develop, and implement innovative course content for LIFE-specific classes focused on career development Conduct career/internship advising meetings as needed Assist students in writing Individualized Learning Agreements (ILAs) and developing GATE (Graduating Alumni Transition Exploration) Plans as they pertain to students' career goals Student Planning & Support Support individual student needs and provide academic assistance, including planning and organization Implement Person-Centered Planning Monitor student progress and maintain communication with families Assist students with creating resumes, cover letters, Employment Goal Plans, and Employee Snapshots Collect and use data to guide internship and job placement decisions Program & Curriculum Development Create and implement the Employment Guide and Job Continuum Plan Design and oversee internship placements and work sampling sites Develop and review Internship Assessments and Job Evaluations with students Collaborate with IL Coordinator on transition planning and with Academic Coordinator on LIFE student course planning Provide post-program job placement suggestions to students and families Training & Education Train mentors on internship/employment roles during fall and spring orientations Conduct Work-Based Training with students each fall as appropriate Train employers and staff on Disability Etiquette and the employment component of UL LIFE Host annual training for all employment partnerships Partnership & Employer Engagement Form and maintain employment partnerships through outreach and relationship-building Host informational meetings with potential employers Conduct regular employer follow-ups, gather feedback, and provide support Mentorship & Oversight Observe job sites and provide feedback to employment mentors Oversee and support assigned employment-focused graduate assistant Student & Alumni Engagement Oversee Learn with LIFE – Community Conversations Serve as a GATE (Graduating Alumni Transition Exploration) Plan team member Events & Engagement Plan and participate in programmatic events (Orientation, Preview Day, Interviews, Trainings, Graduation, Recruiting) Represent UL LIFE at university functions and support student campus involvement Participate in staff engagement opportunities and professional development opportunities (e.g., SEPSEA, SOTA) Serve on-call in assigned rotation Collaboration & Communication Maintain effective communication with staff, team members, and Director Consult with peers and Director on student support strategies Introduce program contacts and collaborators to colleagues as appropriate Marketing & Outreach Assist in developing marketing and publicity materials for target audiences Create employment-related content for newsletters and social media related to courses and domain areas Respond to inquiries about the UL LIFE program Other Responsibilities Perform other duties as assigned Qualifications: Master's degree in education, special education, or related field Experience working with and educating individuals with intellectual and developmental disabilities Preferred Qualifications: Teaching certification in education or special education Experience working with special education or inclusive postsecondary education Experience developing and assessing educational curriculum Experience working with career development or employment assistance programs/services Supervision experience Job Ad# (req4572) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
    },
    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4475?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Student Career Development",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Student Career Development | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Director, Student Career Development Lafayette, LA | req4475 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/14/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Assistant Director, Student Career Development Department : 3120|Career Services Responsibilities : Position Summary The Assistant Director of Student Career Development\nprovides high-level, specialized career coaching and tactical program\nleadership within the University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s Office of Career\nServices. The Assistant Director reports to the Director and leads the design\nand delivery of high-impact job search resources and industry-based learning\ninitiatives, working in close coordination with faculty and Employer Engagement\nstaff. By executing creative outreach, programming, and student engagement strategies,\nthis role ensures that students across their designated colleges are\ncompetitively positioned for internships, co-ops, and post-graduation career\nsuccess within the framework of the university’s Student Success Vision. Key Responsibilities: Internship & Job Search Leadership and Resources\nOversight · Coordinate the development and delivery of high-impact\nworkshops and digital resources focused on the end-to-end job search process. · Direct initiatives centered on resume optimization,\ninterview mastery, and strategic search for internships and co-ops\nopportunities including providing the day-to-day supervision of a graduate\nassistant. · Oversee the integration, tracking, documenting, and\naccessibility of university-wide job search platforms (e.g. Handshake). · Monitor usage data and troubleshoot day-to-day technical\naccess issues for job search tools to provide recommendations for actionable\ninsights for resource allocation and procurement decisions. Experiential Learning Coordination · Partner with faculty and Employer Engagement staff to\nidentify, promote, and expand experiential learning opportunities for students. · Oversee the tracking and documenting of experiential\nlearning opportunities and student engagement. · Collaborate on the integration of experiential learning\nmilestones into the student’s academic and co-curricular journey. · Serve as a primary functional point of contact for\nacademic departments, student organizations, and student affairs areas to\noperationalize cross-departmental collaborations for job search and\nindustry-based learning initiatives as needed (e.g. networking events) Career Closet Operations & Resource Management · Manage all Career Closet functions, including coordinating\ndonation drives, overseeing quality control for incoming professional attire,\nand implementing a tracking system to maintain a high-quality, accessible\nresource for students. · Coordinate student staffing by overseeing hiring,\nonboarding, and weekly scheduling while co-developing a specialized training\ncurriculum focused on professional styling, customer service best practice, and\noperational efficiency. Student Engagement & Outreach Execution · Implement creative job preparation and job search\nworkshops, outreach initiatives and career programming designed to increase\nstudent participation in career services from their first semester through\ngraduation. · Represent Career Services at recruitment events, faculty\nmeetings, and student organization events to embed career readiness into\ncollege culture as needed. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Director to\nsupport the mission and success of Career Services for students and alumni. Qualifications: Required Qualications: Education Requires a bachelor’s degree in business, marketing,\npsychology, communication, public relations, or other related areas. Preferred\n- Master’s degree in counseling, higher education administration, or related\narea. Experience -Minimum three (3) years of experience within career\ndevelopment, counseling, higher education, human resources, academic advising,\nor other relevant corporate and community experience. -Proven knowledge of career development theories, career\nreadiness, and career counseling skills. Experience utilizing Clifton\nStrengths, Type Focus, Choices 360 are a plus. -Experience and ability creating and sustaining collaborative\nrelationships with departments, organizations, or student groups. ---Ability to\neffectively interact with faculty, staff, students, parents, and\nadministrators. -Experience developing educational programs for large and\nsmall audiences. -Excellent oral and written communication skills; ability to\nspeak effectively before groups. -Must be a self-starter and possess strong analytical and\nproblem-solving skills. Demonstrated ability to organize and work independently\nas a leader and as part of a team. -Should be able to work nights and weekends as needed. Job Ad# (req4475) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
    },
    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4537?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Sports Medicine",
      "description": "Associate Director of Sports Medicine | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Associate Director of Sports Medicine Lafayette, LA | req4537 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/28/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Associate Director of Sports Medicine Department : 8913|Sports Medicine Responsibilities : The University of Louisiana at Lafayette is\nseeking qualified candidates for an Associate Director of Sports Medicine. This\nposition reports directly to the Assistant Director of Athletics for Sports\nMedicine and has direct supervision of Assistant Directors of Sports Medicine\nand Certified Intern Athletic Trainers. Assists the Assistant Director of\nAthletics for Sports Medicine with the provision of athletic training services\nincluding prevention, care, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries for 16\nintercollegiate sports and spirit squads. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBLITIES -Assists the Assistant Director of Athletics for Sports Medicine in the supervision of the Athletic Training Room. -Coordinates health care with team physicians. -Reports the status of injured student athletes to coaching staff. -Assists with yearly scheduling and administration of student-athlete physical exams and testing. -Provides first aid and emergency care for athletic related injuries. -Provides coverage with home and away events. -Maintains medical and insurance records. -Maintains inventory and supplies. -Recruits and supervises student trainers. -May include teaching duties. -Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: REQUIRED EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE -Bachelor's degree from a regionally accredited institution -Current NATABOC certification -Current CPR/AED certification -Current Louisiana State Board of Medical Examiners Athletic Training Licensure (or eligible for licensure) -Minimum of 3 years’ experience in providing athletic training services PREFERRED EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE -Master’s degree from a regionally accredited institution -Minimum of 3 years’ experience in providing athletic training services at a NCAA Division I university PERFORMANCE EXPECTATIONS: KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS,\nAND ABILITIES -Exhibit excellent written and verbal communication, organizational, public relations, interpersonal, customer service, and supervisory skills when working with student-athletes, faculty, staff, coaches, and administration. -Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others; commitment to working with multi-cultural populations. -Have strong work ethic and be a person of high integrity and character who shares a commitment for knowing and complying with NCAA, Conference, and Institutional rules as they apply to the University of Louisiana at Lafayette Athletics program. -Ability to work extended daily hours, evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed. Job Ad# (req4537) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
    },
    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4498?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Athletic Performance for Football",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Athletic Performance for Football | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Director of Athletic Performance for Football Lafayette, LA | req4498 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/28/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Assistant Director of Athletic Performance for Football Department : 8922|Football Responsibilities : <<External vacancy description>> The University of Louisiana at Lafayette\nAthletics Department is seeking a qualified Assistant Director of Athletic\nPerformance for Football. This position will report directly to the Director of\nAthletic Performance for Football and will work only with the Football team. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES -Assist in the development and implementation of performance programming for the football team, including strength and conditioning, speed and agility, and injury prevention strategies. -Collaborate with the Director of Athletic Performance for Football to develop individualized training programs for football student-athletes to maximize performance and minimize injury risk. -Oversee the Athletic Performance Assistant for Football and the Athletic Performance interns, providing guidance and feedback as necessary. -Monitor the progress of football student-athletes, regularly assessing their physical development and making necessary adjustments to their training programs. -Work with the coaching staff to ensure that the performance program is integrated effectively with the team's practice and game schedule. -Collaborate with the Athletic Training and Sports Medicine staff to ensure that football student-athletes are receiving appropriate care and rehabilitation for injuries. -Stay up-to-date on current research and best practices in athletic performance, attending professional development opportunities as necessary. -Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletic Performance for Football. Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS -Bachelor’s degree from a regionally accredited institution. -1 year of collegiate athletic/sports performance or comparable experience required. -Must be certified by the Collegiate Strength and Conditioning Coaches Association (CSCCA) or the National Strength and Conditioning Association (NSCA) as a Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist (CSCS) and current on CPR/AED and first aid certification. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS -Bachelor’s degree in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, or related field. -Master’s degree from a regionally accredited institution. -Exhibit excellent written and verbal communication, organizational, public relations, interpersonal, customer service, and supervisory skills when working with student-athletes, faculty, staff, coaches, and administration. -Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others; commitment to working with multi-cultural populations. -Have strong work ethic and be a person of high integrity and character who shares a commitment for knowing and complying with NCAA, Conference, and Institutional rules as they apply to the University of Louisiana at Lafayette Athletics program. -Ability to work extended daily hours, evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed. Job Ad# (req4498) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
