    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4592?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Director of Advancement Technology",
      "description": "Director of Advancement Technology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Director of Advancement Technology Lafayette, LA | req4592 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/23/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Director of Advancement Technology Department : 7040|University Advancement Responsibilities : The Director of Advancement Technology serves as the lead technical position for University Advancement, providing leadership for Advancement systems, databases, reporting, integrations, data governance, and technology initiatives. The Director leads a technical team and partners with Advancement leadership, Central IT, the UL Foundation, and campus stakeholders to develop and maintain technology solutions supporting fundraising and Advancement operations. The position serves as the functional and technical administrator and subject matter expert for Ellucian CRM Advance and is responsible for the effective, secure, and strategic use of Advancement technology and data. This is a hands-on technical leadership position that requires experience in diagnosing complex production issues, reviewing and developing SQL and database solutions, evaluating integrations and reporting logic, and providing direct technical support when needed. The person is a lead member of the Advancement Operations team and works cooperatively with other office staff to achieve University and Advancement goals. This position currently reports to the Associate Vice President, Development Responsibilities: · Supervise, mentor, and provide technical leadership to approximately 8–10 staff responsible for Advancement systems, integrations, reporting, and data operations, including technical review, prioritization, cross-training, and staff development. · Lead technology projects through requirements gathering, design, development, testing, implementation, documentation, and ongoing support using Agile/Scrum or other methodologies and project management platforms. · Lead database development, advanced SQL programming, code review, reporting, integrations, automation, and other data solutions supporting Advancement operations. · Provide technical ownership and leadership for CRM Advance and related Advancement applications, including administration, configuration, development, integrations, upgrades, security, troubleshooting, performance, and ongoing enhancement. · Design, oversee, govern, and troubleshoot integrations between CRM Advance, University enterprise systems, fundraising platforms, and third-party applications, including APIs, automated data exchanges, and file-based integrations. · Establish and oversee standards for data governance, data integrity, security, documentation, testing, and system administration. · Analyze Advancement business processes and partner with stakeholders to identify opportunities for improvement and translate business requirements into technical solutions. · Provide technical direction, establish priorities, evaluate technology solutions, and contribute to Advancement's technology strategy and roadmap. · Participate in technology planning, vendor and solution evaluation, software licensing and renewals, contract review, and Advancement technology budgeting. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: · Bachelor's degree in computer science, information systems, business, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. · Five or more years of supervisory, management, or senior technical leadership experience in information technology, enterprise systems, data, or related environment. · Five or more years of technical experience in database development, systems analysis, application development, reporting, integrations, or related information technology functions. · Experience administering, developing, implementing, or supporting enterprise systems such as CRM, ERP, fundraising, or other business-critical applications. · Demonstrated advanced proficiency in SQL and relational database development, including T-SQL in Microsoft SQL Server, complex queries, stored procedures, data transformation, troubleshooting, and performance optimization. Preferred Qualifications: · Master's degree. · PMP certification or comparable project management credentials. · Experience with Ellucian CRM Advance, Ellucian Banner ERP, or other higher education enterprise systems. · Experience in philanthropy, fundraising, development, or nonprofit advancement, with knowledge of constituent management, gift and pledge processing, prospect management, and related business processes; higher education Advancement experience is preferred. · Experience with reporting and business intelligence technologies such as Crystal Reports, Power BI, or comparable platforms. · Experience with Microsoft Power Platform, JavaScript, JSON/XML, web technologies, APIs, cloud storage/services, and web-based or enterprise integrations. Job Ad# (req4592) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
