    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4605?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Instructor",
      "description": "Instructor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Instructor Lafayette, LA | req4605 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/20/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Instructor Department : 2610|Nursing Responsibilities : The Nursing Faculty Member for the Bachelor\nof Science in Nursing (BSN) Program plays a crucial role in providing\nhigh-quality education to future nurses. This position focuses on classroom and\nclinical teaching, academic advising, and active involvement in academic and\nservice-related activities. The ideal candidate will exhibit a commitment to\nongoing intellectual competence and professional development. Key Responsibilities: -Develop and deliver engaging, up-to-date, and evidence-based\nlectures, discussions, and activities for nursing courses. Foster a positive and inclusive learning environment that\nsupports student success. -Utilize technology and interactive teaching methods to\nenhance student learning in a competitive, technology-based learning\nenvironment. -Provide clinical instruction and supervision to nursing\nstudents in healthcare settings. -Ensure that students receive hands-on training, guidance, and\nsupport to develop clinical competencies. -Collaborate with healthcare facilities to coordinate clinical\nplacements and ensure adherence to program requirements. -Assist students in developing individualized academic plans\nto meet their educational and professional aspirations. -Engage in ongoing professional development activities,\nincluding research, attending conferences, and staying current with\nadvancements in nursing education and practice. -Contribute to the development of innovative teaching methods\nand curriculum enhancement. -Participate actively in department and university committees,\nas well as community engagement initiatives. -Collaborate with colleagues to improve program quality,\nassessment, and accreditation efforts. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: An earned master’s degree in nursing is\nrequired and previous experience teaching at the BSN and/or MSN level is\npreferred.  Must be licensed as a Registered Nurse in Louisiana or\neligible for licensure.  Successful candidates must be committed to\nworking effectively with diverse student populations. Applicants are expected\nto describe their commitment to fostering a diverse educational environment\nthrough their everyday communication with students and faculty and/or service\nactivities. Job Ad# (req4605) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
