    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4597?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Resource Coordinator",
      "description": "Resource Coordinator | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Resource Coordinator Lafayette, LA | req4597 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/19/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Resource Coordinator Department : 9070|IMRi Responsibilities : Responsibilities: Under the supervision of the Director of the Institute for Materials Research and Innovation the Resource Coordinator: independently manages the business function (managing budget, overseeing R&D grant expenditures, upgrading of the labs and facilities, managing hires, planning events, etc.) of the various research projects. Independently manages research facility maintenance and improvement projects, including procurement, and asset management.  Provides information to the Director concerning Institute oversight, including the tracking, forecasting, and managing of institute-wide and grant-speciﬁc timelines, milestones and budgets. Assists in the coordination of student involvement in research projects.  Helps prepare federal, state, and foundation grant applications in collaboration with research investigators. Assists in the development of instructional materials. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: -B.S. degree is required with preference for a degree in a STEM field -Experience with accounting and finance -Experience with community engagement -Experience with applying technical concepts toward solving problems -Experience with writing and editing technical documents Skills, Abilities, Etc: -Written and verbal communication skills -Interpersonal/human relations skills -Organizational and analytical skills -Ability to maintain conﬁdentiality Job Ad# (req4597) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title