    "https://louisiana.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/4526?c=louisiana": {
      "title": "Area Coordinator",
      "description": "Area Coordinator | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Area Coordinator Lafayette, LA | req4526 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/19/2026 Back to Search Position Title : Area Coordinator Department : Division of Student Success Responsibilities : <<External vacancy description>> Area Coordinator Position Summary The Area Coordinator is responsible for fostering a vibrant,\nsupportive, inclusive, and life-enhancing residential environment that promotes\nstudent learning, engagement, and personal development. Working collaboratively\nwith the Office of Residential Life and the Office of University Housing, the\nArea Coordinator provides leadership and oversight for an assigned residential\narea and contributes to the overall residential experience of approximately\n3,500 students. The Area Coordinator oversees an assigned area of\napproximately 1,000–1,500 residents and provides leadership, supervision, and\nsupport to professional and student staff within the area. This position plays\na key role in the recruitment, selection, onboarding, training, supervision,\nand development of residential staff. The Area Coordinator is required to live in an on-campus\napartment and maintain availability during evening, weekend, and\nnon-traditional hours. The position provides direct support to students and\nstaff, responds to emergency and non-emergency situations, and connects\nstudents with appropriate campus resources to address academic, personal, and\ndevelopmental needs. The Area Coordinator works closely with Housing and\nResidential Life staff to support daily operations, community engagement,\nstudent success, and the overall safety and well-being of the residential\ncommunity. The Area Coordinator reports directly to the Director of Residential\nLife. General Expectations & Responsibilities -Supervise,\n     train, and develop Resident Assistants, Community Directors, and Assistant\n     Community Directors. -Lead\n     and support the recruitment, selection, onboarding, training, scheduling,\n     and ongoing development of residential staff. -Provide\n     consistent supervision, coaching, feedback, and accountability to student\n     and professional staff. -Uphold\n     and enforce University, Housing, and Residential Life policies and\n     procedures. -Respond\n     appropriately to emergency and non-emergency situations and engage\n     appropriate campus resources when additional assistance is needed. -Manage\n     residential conduct cases as assigned by the Director of Student Rights\n     and Responsibilities. -Advise\n     and support the Residence Hall Association (RHA) and National Residence\n     Hall Honorary (NRHH). -Live\n     in an assigned on-campus apartment and maintain availability during\n     non-traditional hours. -Collaborate\n     with Building Managers and Housing staff to coordinate room assignments,\n     room moves, check-ins, check-outs, and other housing operations. -Participate\n     in the University's divisional on-call rotation. -Serve\n     as a visible and engaged presence within the residential communities. -Build\n     relationships with residents and staff and promote a strong sense of\n     community, belonging, and connection. Student Services & Leadership -Maintain\n     a welcoming, supportive, and student-centered environment for residents,\n     guests, staff, and visitors. -Be\n     visible and maintain office hours. Be able to work evening hours for attending\n     programs. -Serve in\n     an on-call duty rotation for all of campus. In addition, serve on call on\n     a weekly basis for Residential Life. -Provide\n     leadership and oversight for a residential area of approximately\n     1,000–1,500 students. -Maintain\n     a high level of professionalism in communication and interactions with\n     students, families, staff, University partners, and visitors. -Promote\n     a safe and secure residential environment by identifying and reporting\n     suspicious, threatening, or concerning activity to the appropriate\n     University personnel. -Support\n     student academic success through residential programming, intentional\n     engagement, referrals, and collaboration with campus partners. -Develop\n     and implement programs, initiatives, and engagement opportunities that\n     support student learning, leadership, wellness, belonging, and community\n     development. -Advise\n     departmental committees and initiatives, which may include Sustainability,\n     Diversity, Academics, Intramurals, and Community Service. -Serve\n     on University-wide committees and collaborate with departments and offices\n     across the Division of Student Affairs. -Develop\n     collaborative relationships with campus partners to enhance the student\n     residential experience. -Support\n     student leadership development and encourage meaningful student\n     involvement within the residential community. Administrative & Operational Responsibilities -Assist\n     with Housing operational responsibilities, including check-ins,\n     check-outs, room transitions, building turn, and other high-volume\n     operational periods. -Manage\n     and monitor an assigned programming budget and ensure responsible use of\n     departmental funds. -Complete\n     required documentation and administrative processes related to\n     programming, travel, purchasing, staffing, and residential operations. -Attend\n     required staff meetings, trainings, and departmental meetings. -Participate\n     in staff scheduling and operational planning. -Oversee\n     all of the behavioral Maxient cases -Maintain\n     accurate records and complete required reports and documentation in a\n     timely manner. -Meet\n     regularly with the Director of Residential Life or assigned supervisor for\n     supervision, professional development, and performance feedback. -Assist\n     with departmental initiatives, projects, and special events as assigned. -Perform\n     other duties as assigned by the Director of Residential Life or designated\n     University leadership. Successful candidates will demonstrate: -A\n     strong commitment to student development and the residential learning\n     experience. -Creativity\n     and initiative in developing innovative programs and engagement\n     opportunities. -Strong\n     leadership and supervisory skills. -The\n     ability to provide effective coaching, feedback, and accountability to\n     student and professional staff. -Sound\n     judgment and the ability to remain calm and effective during emergency and\n     crisis situations. -Strong\n     organizational and administrative skills. -Excellent\n     communication and relationship-building skills. -A\n     proactive, energetic, collaborative, and student-centered approach. -Commitment to creating residential communities\nwhere students feel safe, connected, supported, and empowered to succeed Area Coordinator Position Summary The Area Coordinator is responsible for fostering a vibrant,\nsupportive, inclusive, and life-enhancing residential environment that promotes\nstudent learning, engagement, and personal development. Working collaboratively\nwith the Office of Residential Life and the Office of University Housing, the\nArea Coordinator provides leadership and oversight for an assigned residential\narea and contributes to the overall residential experience of approximately\n3,500 students. The Area Coordinator oversees an assigned area of\napproximately 1,000–1,500 residents and provides leadership, supervision, and\nsupport to professional and student staff within the area. This position plays\na key role in the recruitment, selection, onboarding, training, supervision,\nand development of residential staff. The Area Coordinator is required to live in an on-campus\napartment and maintain availability during evening, weekend, and\nnon-traditional hours. The position provides direct support to students and\nstaff, responds to emergency and non-emergency situations, and connects\nstudents with appropriate campus resources to address academic, personal, and\ndevelopmental needs. The Area Coordinator works closely with Housing and\nResidential Life staff to support daily operations, community engagement,\nstudent success, and the overall safety and well-being of the residential\ncommunity. The Area Coordinator reports directly to the Director of Residential\nLife. General Expectations & Responsibilities Supervise,\n     train, and develop Resident Assistants, Community Directors, and Assistant\n     Community Directors. Lead\n     and support the recruitment, selection, onboarding, training, scheduling,\n     and ongoing development of residential staff. Provide\n     consistent supervision, coaching, feedback, and accountability to student\n     and professional staff. Uphold\n     and enforce University, Housing, and Residential Life policies and\n     procedures. Respond\n     appropriately to emergency and non-emergency situations and engage\n     appropriate campus resources when additional assistance is needed. Manage\n     residential conduct cases as assigned by the Director of Student Rights\n     and Responsibilities. Advise\n     and support the Residence Hall Association (RHA) and National Residence\n     Hall Honorary (NRHH). Live\n     in an assigned on-campus apartment and maintain availability during\n     non-traditional hours. Collaborate\n     with Building Managers and Housing staff to coordinate room assignments,\n     room moves, check-ins, check-outs, and other housing operations. Participate\n     in the University's divisional on-call rotation. Serve\n     as a visible and engaged presence within the residential communities. Build\n     relationships with residents and staff and promote a strong sense of\n     community, belonging, and connection. Student Services & Leadership Maintain\n     a welcoming, supportive, and student-centered environment for residents,\n     guests, staff, and visitors. Be\n     visible and maintain office hours. Be able to work evening hours for attending\n     programs. Serve in\n     an on-call duty rotation for all of campus. In addition, serve on call on\n     a weekly basis for Residential Life. Provide\n     leadership and oversight for a residential area of approximately\n     1,000–1,500 students. Maintain\n     a high level of professionalism in communication and interactions with\n     students, families, staff, University partners, and visitors. Promote\n     a safe and secure residential environment by identifying and reporting\n     suspicious, threatening, or concerning activity to the appropriate\n     University personnel. Support\n     student academic success through residential programming, intentional\n     engagement, referrals, and collaboration with campus partners. Develop\n     and implement programs, initiatives, and engagement opportunities that\n     support student learning, leadership, wellness, belonging, and community\n     development. Advise\n     departmental committees and initiatives, which may include Sustainability,\n     Diversity, Academics, Intramurals, and Community Service. Serve\n     on University-wide committees and collaborate with departments and offices\n     across the Division of Student Affairs. Develop\n     collaborative relationships with campus partners to enhance the student\n     residential experience. Support\n     student leadership development and encourage meaningful student\n     involvement within the residential community. Administrative & Operational Responsibilities Assist\n     with Housing operational responsibilities, including check-ins,\n     check-outs, room transitions, building turn, and other high-volume\n     operational periods. Manage\n     and monitor an assigned programming budget and ensure responsible use of\n     departmental funds. Complete\n     required documentation and administrative processes related to\n     programming, travel, purchasing, staffing, and residential operations. Attend\n     required staff meetings, trainings, and departmental meetings. Participate\n     in staff scheduling and operational planning. Oversee\n     all of the behavioral Maxient cases Maintain\n     accurate records and complete required reports and documentation in a\n     timely manner. Meet\n     regularly with the Director of Residential Life or assigned supervisor for\n     supervision, professional development, and performance feedback. Assist\n     with departmental initiatives, projects, and special events as assigned. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director\nof Residential Life or designated Qualifications: Required Qualifications: -Bachelor's\n     degree from a regionally accredited institution required. Preferred Qualifications: -Master's\n     degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, College Student\n     Development, or a related field preferred. -Professional\n     or graduate-level experience in Residence Life, Housing, Student Affairs,\n     or a related field preferred. -Experience\n     with student staff supervision, residential programming, student conduct,\n     crisis response, or community development preferred. Skills, Abilities, Etc: -Strong\n     written, verbal, interpersonal, organizational, and problem-solving\n     skills. -Ability\n     to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and work effectively in a\n     fast-paced residential environment. -Demonstrated\n     commitment to student development, community building, and student\n     success. -Ability\n     to work independently while also functioning effectively as part of a\n     collaborative team. -Ability\n     and willingness to work evening, weekend, and non-traditional hours,\n     including participation in an on-call rotation. -Ability\n     to live in an assigned on-campus apartment and respond to residential\n     emergencies as required. Bachelor's\n     degree from a regionally accredited institution required. Master's\n     degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, College Student\n     Development, or a related field preferred. Professional\n     or graduate-level experience in Residence Life, Housing, Student Affairs,\n     or a related field preferred. Experience\n     with student staff supervision, residential programming, student conduct,\n     crisis response, or community development preferred. Strong\n     written, verbal, interpersonal, organizational, and problem-solving\n     skills. Ability\n     to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and work effectively in a\n     fast-paced residential environment. Demonstrated\n     commitment to student development, community building, and student\n     success. Ability\n     to work independently while also functioning effectively as part of a\n     collaborative team. Ability\n     and willingness to work evening, weekend, and non-traditional hours,\n     including participation in an on-call rotation. Ability\n     to live in an assigned on-campus apartment and respond to residential\n     emergencies as required. Job Ad# (req4526) Apply Now Share Save Job The University of Louisiana at Lafayette does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities as required by Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, Age Discrimination Act of 1975, the Equal Pay Act of 1963, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Section 402 of the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 and the 1990 Americans With Disabilities Act. The University of Louisiana\nat Lafayette serves as a model employer (or SAME) related to the employment of individuals with disabilities and is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. If you require reasonable accommodation in\ncompleting this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment\ntesting, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please contact\nthe ADA Coordinator in the Office of Human Resources at (337) 482-1014 or email: hrcompliance@louisiana.edu. You may also complete an ADA Reasonable Accommodations Request Form for Employees & Applicants by clicking the following link: https://cm.maxient.com/reportingform.php?UnivofLouisiana&layout_id=10. General inquiries about posted vacancies should be directed to the hiring department.  If you have any technical issues, trouble accessing your Career Site profile or completing the online application, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@louisiana.edu or (337) 482-6242. Information about the University is available on the University's web page at https://www.louisiana.edu Additional information about our Academic areas can be found at https://louisiana.edu/about-us/offices/academic-affairs . University of Louisiana at Lafayette Annual Security Report: The University of Louisiana at Lafayette’s annual security report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those related to alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act, a copy of the annual security report is available below: Annual Security and Fire Safety\nReport A hard copy may be obtained by contacting the UL Police Department at (337) 482-6447."
